27
00:01:43,190 --> 00:01:46,370
[Previously on Knot]

28
00:01:43,259 --> 00:01:45,229
Don't be afraid. No matter what happens,

29
00:01:45,229 --> 00:01:46,380
I will stay with Phatsa.

30
00:01:46,380 --> 00:01:47,970
A Pure Omega's body

31
00:01:47,990 --> 00:01:49,460
is much stronger than a normal Omega's.

32
00:01:49,460 --> 00:01:50,310
Pure Omega?

33
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:52,320
Is Phatsa a Pure Omega?

34
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:55,350
Do you remember this person?

35
00:01:55,380 --> 00:01:57,620
I saw her at the bar that night.

36
00:01:59,729 --> 00:02:01,390
But I don't remember clearly.

37
00:02:01,550 --> 00:02:03,290
Someone walked over and bumped into me that night.

38
00:02:03,290 --> 00:02:06,530
But the photos the police used to accuse you

39
00:02:07,130 --> 00:02:08,330
are these photos.

40
00:02:09,330 --> 00:02:11,020
And looking at the photos,

41
00:02:11,050 --> 00:02:13,200
you and that woman acted very intimately,

42
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:16,100
as if you willingly stayed with her all the time.

43
00:02:23,460 --> 00:02:25,220
These photos are too coincidental.

44
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:26,079
Exactly.

45
00:02:27,060 --> 00:02:28,950
These were not taken continuously,

46
00:02:28,950 --> 00:02:33,010
but someone deliberately chose the most easily misunderstood moments.

47
00:02:34,930 --> 00:02:36,690
That means

48
00:02:36,710 --> 00:02:41,200
the photographer knew exactly what timing to wait for.

49
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:46,560
And the timestamps on the photos are also weird.

50
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:51,740
Some photos are clearly only minutes apart,

51
00:02:51,770 --> 00:02:53,700
but the people around in the photos

52
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:55,579
are completely different, as if a part of the scene

53
00:02:55,579 --> 00:02:57,110
was deliberately deleted.

54
00:02:58,360 --> 00:02:59,820
Phatsa, what did you find?

55
00:03:01,110 --> 00:03:05,050
The shooting angle of this one and this one

56
00:03:05,070 --> 00:03:07,250
is almost in the same position.

57
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,760
If the photographer was just a normal customer

58
00:03:11,790 --> 00:03:13,730
standing in the bar for so long,

59
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:16,760
and no one ever passed by to block the view...

60
00:03:16,760 --> 00:03:17,560
You mean...

61
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:19,570
It means

62
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:23,890
the photographer wasn't shooting randomly at all,

63
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:27,160
but found a position in advance,

64
00:03:27,190 --> 00:03:30,300
or someone specifically kept the view clear for them.

65
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:32,210
If so,

66
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:33,380
then the content presented in these photos

67
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:34,440
is all misleading.

68
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:37,610
Or rather,

69
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:41,900
someone deliberately caused misunderstandings from the very beginning.

70
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:47,070
So, these evidence photos we got

71
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:49,960
are not a coincidence at all.

72
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:54,130
It's more like a setup.

73
00:03:57,500 --> 00:03:58,800
That means

74
00:03:58,820 --> 00:04:01,750
someone has been targeting Naphitch for a long time.

75
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:04,360
This is no longer just an ordinary frame-up.

76
00:04:06,010 --> 00:04:08,200
I think this is an organized

77
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:10,150
and planned systematic frame-up.

78
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:13,060
So, I remembered it right.

79
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,000
That night, someone really approached me on purpose.

80
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:21,250
Right, but it seems

81
00:04:21,269 --> 00:04:24,830
they don't just want to hurt you.

82
00:04:24,830 --> 00:04:28,230
They want to use this whole thing

83
00:04:28,250 --> 00:04:31,060
to drag the Devathitirat family down.

84
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:36,480
So, this isn't a personal grudge, right?

85
00:04:36,970 --> 00:04:37,770
Right.

86
00:04:39,340 --> 00:04:41,340
This is a formal declaration of war.

87
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:43,520
And whoever started this

88
00:04:43,550 --> 00:04:47,360
must be very confident they can take on our family.

89
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:49,760
But they miscalculated,

90
00:04:49,790 --> 00:04:51,720
because Mr. Naphitch is not alone.

91
00:04:57,600 --> 00:04:58,659
Have a drink.

92
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:01,400
This matter,

93
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:05,730
we need to think it over carefully.

94
00:05:15,290 --> 00:05:16,090
Sila.

95
00:05:16,110 --> 00:05:16,910
Yes.

96
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:19,810
Check Mai's financial transactions thoroughly.

97
00:05:19,810 --> 00:05:21,750
And pull up all the security footage

98
00:05:21,750 --> 00:05:23,510
from the bar on the night of the incident.

99
00:05:23,510 --> 00:05:25,510
If these photos were really staged,

100
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:28,960
they must have left some flaws.

101
00:05:32,900 --> 00:05:33,700
Understood.

102
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:37,200
Nakhin, Ai, check if there have been

103
00:05:37,220 --> 00:05:38,720
any suspicious people

104
00:05:38,750 --> 00:05:40,750
hanging around our house recently,

105
00:05:41,250 --> 00:05:45,409
especially those who might benefit from this.

106
00:05:46,140 --> 00:05:46,940
Understood.

107
00:05:49,650 --> 00:05:54,780
You don't have to remember everything at once.

108
00:05:55,820 --> 00:06:00,250
Just tell us whatever comes to mind,

109
00:06:00,270 --> 00:06:02,530
and we'll help you investigate the rest.

110
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:04,100
Okay.

111
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:09,120
Phatsa.

112
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:12,200
If Phatsa hadn't noticed

113
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:14,000
the issue with the camera angle,

114
00:06:14,380 --> 00:06:16,130
we probably

115
00:06:16,150 --> 00:06:18,880
would have been led by these illusions all along.

116
00:06:19,990 --> 00:06:24,820
I just don't want innocent people

117
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:28,690
who did nothing wrong to get hurt for no reason.

118
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:47,400
Wait, I think I've seen this necklace somewhere.

119
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:49,659
Where have you seen it?

120
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:51,920
If I remember correctly,

121
00:06:51,940 --> 00:06:56,480
it should be Saengnuea's.

122
00:06:58,060 --> 00:06:59,920
If it's really the same necklace,

123
00:07:00,700 --> 00:07:01,470
that means Saengnuea

124
00:07:01,470 --> 00:07:03,330
was definitely at the bar that night,

125
00:07:03,330 --> 00:07:04,960
and it wasn't a coincidence.

126
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:07,660
Because the position she was in

127
00:07:07,660 --> 00:07:08,860
is exactly where the person who took these photos

128
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:09,860
was standing.

129
00:07:11,130 --> 00:07:14,600
If so, she might not just be a witness.

130
00:07:14,960 --> 00:07:16,760
Maybe from the very beginning,

131
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:19,780
she was involved in setting all this up.

132
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:23,560
But she shouldn't have any reason to do this to me.

133
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:26,400
But sometimes,

134
00:07:29,330 --> 00:07:31,190
the people who can hurt us the most

135
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,400
are exactly the ones

136
00:07:36,130 --> 00:07:38,060
we never thought to guard against.

137
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:41,960
If Saengnuea is really involved,

138
00:07:42,210 --> 00:07:45,950
then this is more complicated than we thought.

139
00:07:47,470 --> 00:07:50,500
That means the people around Naphitch

140
00:07:52,400 --> 00:07:54,640
might have been sent to him from the start.

141
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:58,480
Or maybe they just used her as a cover

142
00:07:58,510 --> 00:08:00,780
to make Naphitch lower his guard.

143
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:04,640
If that's true,

144
00:08:04,670 --> 00:08:06,870
Mai might not be the mastermind either.

145
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,900
She might just be a pawn.

146
00:08:13,390 --> 00:08:14,420
It's as if

147
00:08:15,670 --> 00:08:17,040
these photos aren't just targeting

148
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:19,510
Naphitch at all,

149
00:08:20,390 --> 00:08:22,990
but someone carefully orchestrated all this.

150
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:24,470
That person knew the timing well

151
00:08:24,470 --> 00:08:26,070
and knew where Naphitch was.

152
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:28,320
We can't jump to conclusions yet.

153
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:30,700
But one thing is certain,

154
00:08:31,330 --> 00:08:31,940
Saengnuea

155
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:33,090
is another suspect.

156
00:08:34,970 --> 00:08:39,350
Then I'll send someone to check that necklace immediately,

157
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:40,880
and also check Saengnuea's

158
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:43,210
whereabouts on the night of the incident.

159
00:08:43,700 --> 00:08:45,170
I will continue to investigate how she and Mai

160
00:08:45,170 --> 00:08:47,200
got in touch with each other.

161
00:08:47,220 --> 00:08:50,760
If it's a team effort, they will definitely leave a trace.

162
00:08:52,530 --> 00:08:55,010
I will review the entire timeline,

163
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:58,600
from before the incident to after it was exposed.

164
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:01,340
If Saengnuea is really involved,

165
00:09:01,340 --> 00:09:04,140
there will definitely be more than one trace left.

166
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:07,560
If Saengnuea is really related to this matter,

167
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:12,730
I will never let him hurt anyone in this family again.

168
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:37,360
Hello, what's wrong, Phatsa?

169
00:09:38,530 --> 00:09:39,760
Ongsa.

170
00:09:39,780 --> 00:09:42,460
The Devathitirat family is in a mess right now.

171
00:09:44,610 --> 00:09:45,950
And this morning,

172
00:09:45,980 --> 00:09:48,810
I also had a conflict with Nakhun's father.

173
00:09:50,330 --> 00:09:51,760
Has it come to this?

174
00:09:52,330 --> 00:09:53,520
What about Saengnuea?

175
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:55,500
Did he go to the shop to find you?

176
00:09:55,930 --> 00:09:59,780
Saengnuea hasn't come yet.

177
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:04,000
But actually, I had an appointment with him today,

178
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:08,600
but he just messaged me to cancel it.

179
00:10:09,630 --> 00:10:12,860
And he didn't even tell me the reason.

180
00:10:12,880 --> 00:10:17,730
Calm down first. I'll help you check.

181
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:21,560
Ongsa.

182
00:10:22,130 --> 00:10:22,930
Yeah.

183
00:10:23,330 --> 00:10:24,200
What happened?

184
00:10:25,330 --> 00:10:27,060
Something happened to Phatsa.

185
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:45,100
Here, drink some. You'll feel better.

186
00:10:47,330 --> 00:10:48,390
Careful. It's hot.

187
00:11:21,950 --> 00:11:23,240
What are you doing?

188
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:31,560
Phatsa is really amazing.

189
00:11:32,590 --> 00:11:34,720
You can even notice such tiny details.

190
00:11:35,090 --> 00:11:38,200
I usually like to play spot-the-difference games,

191
00:11:39,450 --> 00:11:42,710
so I developed the habit of observing details in pictures.

192
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:51,860
So amazing. Looks like you need a reward.

193
00:11:54,330 --> 00:11:55,200
What reward?

194
00:12:04,460 --> 00:12:05,560
Just a kiss.

195
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:10,850
For someone like you, one kiss won't satisfy you.

196
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:13,800
Just one.

197
00:12:17,660 --> 00:12:18,920
Then kiss on the cheek.

198
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:26,400
Wait a minute.

199
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:32,510
Shouldn't I be the one getting the reward?

200
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,060
You just realized?

201
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:45,300
You really are a wolf in sheep's clothing.

202
00:12:47,930 --> 00:12:49,360
I'm not that cunning.

203
00:12:55,930 --> 00:12:58,190
But you're the one who's so easy to bully.

204
00:13:09,130 --> 00:13:11,330
Occasionally, I should bully you back.

205
00:13:39,690 --> 00:13:44,450
Let's talk about the rest after everything is resolved.

206
00:14:00,660 --> 00:14:01,920
Then solve it quickly.

207
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:30,160
Feeling better?

208
00:14:37,090 --> 00:14:37,890
Much better.

209
00:14:52,860 --> 00:14:53,700
Cheer up.

210
00:15:18,300 --> 00:15:20,460
I came here just to know

211
00:15:20,490 --> 00:15:23,580
who is manipulating Naphitch's matter behind the scenes.

212
00:15:23,580 --> 00:15:26,300
Since you can find this place,

213
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:28,610
you must have found out a lot.

214
00:15:29,730 --> 00:15:32,260
I know this is definitely not a coincidence,

215
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:34,460
and it's related to your people.

216
00:15:39,930 --> 00:15:42,340
This is what I found.

217
00:15:42,370 --> 00:15:46,570
There are transfer records, communication logs,

218
00:15:46,590 --> 00:15:48,670
and a list of related personnel

219
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:50,300
retrieved from the police.

220
00:16:05,760 --> 00:16:07,220
I'll ask you one more time.

221
00:16:07,950 --> 00:16:09,680
Do you know about these things?

222
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:12,060
I don't know.

223
00:16:13,130 --> 00:16:14,860
Then what about this evidence?

224
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:18,730
Your name is in the communication logs,

225
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:20,090
and some of the information

226
00:16:20,090 --> 00:16:21,890
was passed through your people.

227
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:25,310
I admit, in the past, to help you,

228
00:16:25,340 --> 00:16:27,950
I did do some things that crossed the line.

229
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:31,520
But since you told me

230
00:16:31,540 --> 00:16:33,990
you want to conquer everything on your own

231
00:16:34,020 --> 00:16:36,330
and made me believe in your ability,

232
00:16:37,300 --> 00:16:38,960
I let go of everything.

233
00:16:42,240 --> 00:16:44,450
I really have stopped everything.

234
00:16:45,390 --> 00:16:47,560
I just want to support you,

235
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:50,710
and stay by your side in the way you want.

236
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:53,380
I didn't instruct anyone,

237
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:56,420
nor did I do anything behind your back again.

238
00:16:59,160 --> 00:16:59,960
Wait.

239
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:06,530
This surname...

240
00:17:08,290 --> 00:17:09,089
What's wrong?

241
00:17:14,900 --> 00:17:17,030
Kingyok and Mai have the same surname.

242
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:23,750
And it's not just the surname.

243
00:17:23,780 --> 00:17:28,230
According to these documents,

244
00:17:28,810 --> 00:17:30,140
they are cousins.

245
00:17:32,950 --> 00:17:36,580
So, is all of this really

246
00:17:36,610 --> 00:17:38,950
set up by someone in collusion?

247
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:42,200
And it's not just two people.

248
00:17:46,160 --> 00:17:47,490
Did you know about this?

249
00:17:48,130 --> 00:17:51,930
I have nothing to do with Maithong.

250
00:17:53,130 --> 00:17:54,930
Even if we share the same blood,

251
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:57,730
it doesn't mean we're on the same side.

252
00:17:58,300 --> 00:17:59,830
I've never worked with her,

253
00:18:01,130 --> 00:18:03,260
nor have I ever helped her harm anyone.

254
00:18:05,330 --> 00:18:07,060
The only person I am loyal to

255
00:18:11,450 --> 00:18:12,890
is you.

256
00:18:14,060 --> 00:18:20,030
That day you told me you wanted to rely on yourself and asked me to trust you.

257
00:18:21,400 --> 00:18:23,340
I really believed you.

258
00:18:23,370 --> 00:18:25,630
So I stopped everything

259
00:18:25,660 --> 00:18:28,120
and never touched those dirty things again.

260
00:18:29,730 --> 00:18:34,700
I just wanted to stay by your side with dignity.

261
00:18:36,630 --> 00:18:37,800
I believe you.

262
00:18:39,460 --> 00:18:41,760
I really didn't betray you.

263
00:18:41,780 --> 00:18:43,130
Miss Amintra,

264
00:18:44,100 --> 00:18:45,630
please wait outside first.

265
00:18:48,760 --> 00:18:49,560
Okay.

266
00:19:00,360 --> 00:19:01,700
This is no longer just

267
00:19:01,720 --> 00:19:02,920
targeting Naphitch.

268
00:19:03,930 --> 00:19:07,200
They are deliberately approaching us one by one.

269
00:19:08,660 --> 00:19:11,320
Everyone is responsible for different things.

270
00:19:12,100 --> 00:19:14,160
One is responsible for approaching,

271
00:19:14,600 --> 00:19:16,730
one is responsible for setting traps,

272
00:19:16,930 --> 00:19:19,730
and another is responsible for passing messages.

273
00:19:20,260 --> 00:19:21,720
This is an organized gang.

274
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:25,420
The enemy wants to destroy not only our reputation,

275
00:19:26,760 --> 00:19:30,020
but is also infiltrating the people around me step by step.

276
00:19:30,530 --> 00:19:35,730
If they dare to plan so carefully,

277
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:38,760
the goal is probably not just to bring down one person.

278
00:19:39,330 --> 00:19:41,460
They want to destroy the whole family.

279
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:43,160
We must find out

280
00:19:44,360 --> 00:19:45,930
who is behind all this.

281
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:04,150
Your subordinate and the arrested woman have the same surname.

282
00:20:05,550 --> 00:20:07,290
If you are suspecting

283
00:20:07,310 --> 00:20:10,610
whether I am also involved in this,

284
00:20:10,630 --> 00:20:12,400
my answer is

285
00:20:12,580 --> 00:20:14,910
no, it has nothing to do with me.

286
00:20:15,560 --> 00:20:17,740
As for whether you believe it or not,

287
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:21,600
that depends on your common sense and brain.

288
00:20:22,760 --> 00:20:25,670
Since everything can be connected,

289
00:20:25,700 --> 00:20:27,960
why can't I be suspicious?

290
00:20:29,060 --> 00:20:32,180
Mai and Kingyok are indeed cousins,

291
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:34,400
and both are Omegas.

292
00:20:34,430 --> 00:20:37,730
But they didn't grow up together,

293
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:41,530
and they hardly have any sisterly affection.

294
00:20:42,090 --> 00:20:43,290
My family

295
00:20:43,310 --> 00:20:45,810
adopted Kingyok when she was two years old.

296
00:20:47,550 --> 00:20:51,750
But why is it such a coincidence?

297
00:20:52,890 --> 00:20:57,350
I don't know, but if this really happened,

298
00:20:57,380 --> 00:20:59,480
I think there must be

299
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:02,290
someone else connecting them.

300
00:21:04,100 --> 00:21:06,330
Then there is only one person left.

301
00:21:07,590 --> 00:21:11,180
Tim. I heard before

302
00:21:11,200 --> 00:21:14,850
that he was involved in the drug case at your bar,

303
00:21:15,460 --> 00:21:17,630
and was just bailed out not long ago.

304
00:21:17,660 --> 00:21:20,730
That Alpha is Mai's ex-boyfriend.

305
00:21:21,760 --> 00:21:23,020
Is it possible

306
00:21:24,560 --> 00:21:27,790
that Tim deliberately pinned the human trafficking charge

307
00:21:27,790 --> 00:21:29,380
on Naphitch?

308
00:21:31,060 --> 00:21:33,920
He does seem to have a lot of resentment towards you.

309
00:21:40,130 --> 00:21:42,490
By the way, about the land in Chachoengsao,

310
00:21:42,490 --> 00:21:44,420
are you still planning to go see it?

311
00:21:45,140 --> 00:21:47,630
Of course. Amintra,

312
00:21:47,660 --> 00:21:50,580
you said you've already made an appointment with the agent, right?

313
00:21:50,580 --> 00:21:51,380
Yes.

314
00:21:52,380 --> 00:21:54,760
It should be the same person you made an appointment with.

315
00:21:54,760 --> 00:21:56,930
This landlord is too difficult to deal with.

316
00:21:56,930 --> 00:21:59,100
I don't even want to talk to him anymore.

317
00:21:59,100 --> 00:22:00,460
I'm just afraid that when we actually go to negotiate,

318
00:22:00,460 --> 00:22:02,530
he'll suddenly change his mind and refuse to sell.

319
00:22:02,530 --> 00:22:04,330
I'll definitely shoot them all.

320
00:22:05,060 --> 00:22:06,260
That's too ruthless.

321
00:22:16,140 --> 00:22:18,470
Phatsa, let's go home.

322
00:22:40,050 --> 00:22:40,980
Ongsa.

323
00:22:42,300 --> 00:22:43,390
This is Amintra,

324
00:22:43,410 --> 00:22:45,740
the Beta friend I mentioned to you before.

325
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:49,460
Are you really a Beta?

326
00:22:50,360 --> 00:22:52,090
What's wrong with being a Beta?

327
00:22:52,720 --> 00:22:55,870
Amintra made me start to understand

328
00:22:55,890 --> 00:22:58,020
that Betas are not inferior to anyone.

329
00:23:08,160 --> 00:23:10,930
Is this the Beta you like?

330
00:23:15,670 --> 00:23:17,000
Uh.

331
00:23:18,530 --> 00:23:21,660
Looks like you're stuck in the Alpha-Beta romance zone.

332
00:23:25,580 --> 00:23:30,340
How ridiculous. If you think you're a Beta,

333
00:23:30,370 --> 00:23:32,420
then you'll always just be a Beta.

334
00:23:33,560 --> 00:23:36,470
What's so great about Alphas anyway?

335
00:23:36,500 --> 00:23:40,000
Can they fly? Or do their feet catch fire when they walk?

336
00:23:45,960 --> 00:23:47,460
You're really amazing.

337
00:23:47,930 --> 00:23:50,700
This is the way I chose to be.

338
00:23:51,760 --> 00:23:53,330
Whether it's an Alpha,

339
00:23:53,350 --> 00:23:55,360
Omega, or Beta,

340
00:23:55,380 --> 00:23:57,260
none of them can do anything to me,

341
00:23:57,820 --> 00:24:00,480
as long as they are still human.

342
00:24:00,800 --> 00:24:02,860
I'm leaving first.

343
00:24:15,100 --> 00:24:16,900
She just has that kind of temper.

344
00:24:17,560 --> 00:24:18,690
Don't overthink it.

345
00:24:19,860 --> 00:24:21,560
Miss Amintra

346
00:24:21,590 --> 00:24:23,660
is really a cool Beta.

347
00:24:24,800 --> 00:24:26,930
She just likes to show off a bit.

348
00:24:30,930 --> 00:24:33,430
I'll reiterate my view once more.

349
00:24:34,890 --> 00:24:36,140
In my opinion, secondary gender

350
00:24:36,140 --> 00:24:40,170
can never be used to measure a person's worth.

351
00:24:40,200 --> 00:24:42,360
Whether it's Alpha, Omega,

352
00:24:42,390 --> 00:24:45,720
or Beta, in the end, it's just a title.

353
00:24:47,330 --> 00:24:49,530
If I really want to understand someone,

354
00:24:50,730 --> 00:24:52,390
I will look at their true self.

355
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:55,560
I will look at your essence,

356
00:24:57,580 --> 00:24:58,720
look at your heart,

357
00:24:59,800 --> 00:25:02,260
instead of looking at whether you are a Beta.

358
00:25:05,400 --> 00:25:09,700
But you are a member of the Devathitirat family after all.

359
00:25:10,730 --> 00:25:14,860
So what? Does our family grow wings or something?

360
00:25:16,130 --> 00:25:18,130
If I want to stand by someone's side,

361
00:25:19,740 --> 00:25:21,410
that is my own choice,

362
00:25:21,430 --> 00:25:25,280
not because the rules tell me who I should choose.

363
00:25:27,120 --> 00:25:28,970
So,

364
00:25:29,000 --> 00:25:32,000
just because you stand by my side,

365
00:25:32,020 --> 00:25:34,350
you don't have to worry about your status.

366
00:25:36,030 --> 00:25:40,300
Because that has never been an issue for me.

367
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:47,000
Why are you so good with words today?

368
00:25:48,100 --> 00:25:51,160
As long as it's about you, I'm always serious.

369
00:26:05,360 --> 00:26:06,560
Look, here they come.

370
00:26:08,530 --> 00:26:09,330
So slow.

371
00:26:10,660 --> 00:26:12,190
I had to handle a few things.

372
00:26:19,860 --> 00:26:21,660
It's good that everyone is here.

373
00:26:22,200 --> 00:26:25,330
Let's make the important things clear all at once today.

374
00:26:26,260 --> 00:26:29,160
If Father is still going to talk about that matter from before,

375
00:26:29,160 --> 00:26:30,620
my answer will not change.

376
00:26:30,700 --> 00:26:32,190
That Pure Omega child

377
00:26:32,220 --> 00:26:34,300
must become a member of our family.

378
00:26:35,530 --> 00:26:37,790
And you are the most suitable candidate.

379
00:26:39,400 --> 00:26:41,730
I am not a tool to produce heirs for others.

380
00:26:42,730 --> 00:26:44,060
But you are my son,

381
00:26:44,790 --> 00:26:48,200
and you should fulfill the responsibilities consistent with your bloodline.

382
00:26:48,200 --> 00:26:49,300
If Father just wants a Pure

383
00:26:49,300 --> 00:26:51,100
Omega to marry into this family,

384
00:26:52,400 --> 00:26:53,930
then I'll marry them, okay?

385
00:26:55,760 --> 00:26:56,560
You.

386
00:26:57,560 --> 00:26:59,560
If this can put an end to this matter.

387
00:27:00,190 --> 00:27:01,710
From the day you bit Phatsa

388
00:27:01,730 --> 00:27:02,770
and established a mating bond,

389
00:27:02,770 --> 00:27:04,570
you were already disqualified.

390
00:27:04,710 --> 00:27:07,910
A person who ruined their own chances with their own hands

391
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:10,860
has no right to discuss marriage for anyone.

392
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:14,460
What exactly does Father see?

393
00:27:15,960 --> 00:27:18,220
Besides benefits, what else can you see?

394
00:27:18,750 --> 00:27:20,970
What I see is the future of the family.

395
00:27:21,020 --> 00:27:21,820
No.

396
00:27:22,960 --> 00:27:24,620
All Father sees is bloodline,

397
00:27:25,360 --> 00:27:27,100
only the words 'Pure Omega'.

398
00:27:28,100 --> 00:27:29,630
But you never thought about

399
00:27:31,700 --> 00:27:34,100
whether your own children are happy or not.

400
00:27:34,200 --> 00:27:36,130
Happiness is just a fake thing

401
00:27:36,900 --> 00:27:39,900
if it can't make our family stronger.

402
00:27:41,530 --> 00:27:44,330
Then you can keep guarding your strength, Father.

403
00:27:45,500 --> 00:27:46,660
But I will never

404
00:27:48,160 --> 00:27:49,800
hand over my life.

405
00:27:53,860 --> 00:27:55,400
Even if you don't want to,

406
00:27:56,480 --> 00:27:58,080
you will have to do it one day.

407
00:27:59,560 --> 00:28:01,060
As long as I'm still here,

408
00:28:02,930 --> 00:28:04,790
Nakhin won't be forced by anyone.

409
00:28:22,340 --> 00:28:23,350
Are you mad at me?

410
00:28:26,700 --> 00:28:27,730
Who's mad at you?

411
00:28:30,860 --> 00:28:32,190
You're being so formal.

412
00:28:34,060 --> 00:28:35,460
You're clearly mad at me.

413
00:28:40,100 --> 00:28:41,940
Why did you say

414
00:28:41,970 --> 00:28:46,400
you'd marry that Pure Omega for Nakhin?

415
00:29:00,930 --> 00:29:02,590
The only person I want to marry

416
00:29:04,860 --> 00:29:05,900
is Phatsa.

417
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:28,360
The only person I want to marry is Phatsa.

418
00:29:32,730 --> 00:29:34,660
Or does Phatsa not want to marry me?

419
00:29:38,260 --> 00:29:41,130
Who said that? I didn't say anything.

420
00:29:44,230 --> 00:29:46,420
I thought you

421
00:29:46,440 --> 00:29:51,120
were going to marry another Pure Omega for Nakhin.

422
00:30:12,960 --> 00:30:15,000
The only Pure Omega I will marry

423
00:30:16,900 --> 00:30:18,700
is right in front of me, isn't he?

424
00:30:20,560 --> 00:30:23,020
But I don't want Father to know about Phatsa.

425
00:30:23,730 --> 00:30:24,680
I don't want him to know

426
00:30:24,680 --> 00:30:25,420
that Phatsa is the one he's been searching

427
00:30:25,420 --> 00:30:26,550
the whole world for.

428
00:30:29,200 --> 00:30:31,390
I don't want this to be

429
00:30:31,420 --> 00:30:33,960
one of the main reasons he accepts Phatsa.

430
00:30:38,300 --> 00:30:40,000
He wants an Enigma grandson.

431
00:30:42,600 --> 00:30:44,000
And Phatsa is the only one

432
00:30:45,930 --> 00:30:48,190
who is certain to give birth to an Enigma.

433
00:30:52,490 --> 00:30:54,090
I want him to just see Phatsa,

434
00:30:55,530 --> 00:30:58,260
and not let the secondary gender be any part of it.

435
00:31:02,370 --> 00:31:03,460
Also,

436
00:31:06,900 --> 00:31:08,600
Phatsa is mine.

437
00:31:51,960 --> 00:31:53,090
What a coincidence.

438
00:31:54,700 --> 00:31:55,500
Yeah.

439
00:31:57,400 --> 00:32:00,460
It feels like we're meeting more and more often lately.

440
00:32:02,860 --> 00:32:04,290
Or

441
00:32:04,310 --> 00:32:06,730
should I think this isn't a coincidence?

442
00:32:16,020 --> 00:32:17,230
And then?

443
00:32:20,600 --> 00:32:23,460
Do you still want to treat all this as a coincidence?

444
00:32:48,900 --> 00:32:50,700
Let's go sit over there and talk.

445
00:32:51,800 --> 00:32:53,000
Lead the way then.

446
00:33:06,960 --> 00:33:08,560
Have another drink with me,

447
00:33:09,710 --> 00:33:14,290
just to really get to know each other.

448
00:33:22,300 --> 00:33:24,160
Don't we know each other already?

449
00:33:27,410 --> 00:33:28,740
Not yet.

450
00:33:28,760 --> 00:33:34,760
I only know you're a pretty interesting person.

451
00:33:39,400 --> 00:33:40,260
Then let's try.

452
00:33:43,860 --> 00:33:46,170
I like straightforward people.

453
00:33:46,200 --> 00:33:49,200
It's easy to talk to them, and there's no need to guess.

454
00:33:51,160 --> 00:33:54,960
What about you, Mr. Naphitch?

455
00:33:58,300 --> 00:34:01,100
Is it easy for people around you to get close to you?

456
00:34:02,330 --> 00:34:03,460
Depends on who it is.

457
00:34:06,160 --> 00:34:11,360
So if it's someone you trust,

458
00:34:14,960 --> 00:34:17,420
you're willing to let them get close, right?

459
00:34:21,800 --> 00:34:23,860
You really know how to ask questions.

460
00:34:26,060 --> 00:34:28,260
Because I really want to get to know you.

461
00:34:30,420 --> 00:34:34,460
Then next week,

462
00:34:38,300 --> 00:34:40,699
let's spend the whole week together, okay?

463
00:34:43,360 --> 00:34:44,159
Okay?

464
00:34:46,100 --> 00:34:47,989
I'm going out of town next week.

465
00:34:48,400 --> 00:34:51,260
My brothers and I have to deal with some land issues.

466
00:34:51,760 --> 00:34:53,290
Is your whole family going?

467
00:34:54,880 --> 00:34:56,190
Sounds

468
00:34:57,900 --> 00:34:59,100
pretty interesting.

469
00:35:01,460 --> 00:35:02,600
Pretty much.

470
00:35:06,560 --> 00:35:08,100
Can I go with you?

471
00:35:09,830 --> 00:35:10,630
No.

472
00:35:12,260 --> 00:35:14,320
This is our family's private matter.

473
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:16,660
Outsiders are not allowed.

474
00:35:18,190 --> 00:35:18,990
Is that so?

475
00:35:21,370 --> 00:35:23,090
Then,

476
00:35:26,560 --> 00:35:28,560
what if I am Mr. Naphitch's man?

477
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:34,300
Would you let me go then?

478
00:35:39,460 --> 00:35:40,990
Then try being my man first.

479
00:37:40,710 --> 00:37:42,150
Morning tea.

480
00:37:43,430 --> 00:37:46,960
It will make you feel refreshed.

481
00:37:47,200 --> 00:37:48,000
Thank you.

482
00:37:48,340 --> 00:37:49,630
Thank you.

483
00:37:51,640 --> 00:37:53,880
I'll continue cleaning the house.

484
00:37:55,420 --> 00:37:57,420
So the house will be clean and fresh.

485
00:38:00,550 --> 00:38:04,150
Oh, Mr. Naphitch, good morning.

486
00:38:12,850 --> 00:38:15,510
What's wrong? Are you exhausted, little tiger?

487
00:38:16,880 --> 00:38:19,590
Sorry, bro. I overslept.

488
00:38:19,960 --> 00:38:21,260
You made us all late.

489
00:38:23,700 --> 00:38:24,900
Calm down, bro.

490
00:38:25,500 --> 00:38:27,500
The little guy already apologized.

491
00:38:28,160 --> 00:38:28,960
Let's go.

492
00:38:34,530 --> 00:38:36,360
Oh, guys, are you leaving now?

493
00:38:37,160 --> 00:38:39,010
Be careful on the road.

494
00:38:39,150 --> 00:38:40,460
Bye.

495
00:38:40,500 --> 00:38:41,580
See you later.

496
00:38:41,600 --> 00:38:42,940
Goodbye.

497
00:38:52,890 --> 00:38:53,690
Oh.

498
00:38:54,730 --> 00:38:57,130
Do you want to come with us, sister-in-law?

499
00:38:59,000 --> 00:39:00,200
Can I go too?

500
00:39:01,500 --> 00:39:02,960
You'd better stay at home.

501
00:39:03,100 --> 00:39:04,360
It's very hot outside.

502
00:39:08,500 --> 00:39:09,500
Where is it hot?

503
00:39:18,800 --> 00:39:20,330
I'll bring you some snacks.

504
00:39:29,160 --> 00:39:31,160
Are you going with just a few people?

505
00:39:32,190 --> 00:39:35,050
If you mean the bodyguards,

506
00:39:35,070 --> 00:39:37,420
Father has sent them all to find that special person,

507
00:39:37,420 --> 00:39:39,150
so they all have to stay at home.

508
00:39:46,160 --> 00:39:47,260
Go inside first.

509
00:39:48,460 --> 00:39:49,600
See you tonight.

510
00:39:59,500 --> 00:40:00,300
Let's go.

511
00:40:07,530 --> 00:40:08,390
Come on, drive.

512
00:40:10,300 --> 00:40:12,130
Ouch, my arm hurts.

513
00:40:14,500 --> 00:40:15,700
The sun is too strong.

514
00:40:16,000 --> 00:40:16,860
I can't drive.

515
00:40:17,330 --> 00:40:18,130
Drive.

516
00:40:21,300 --> 00:40:22,360
I'll drive myself.

517
00:40:23,070 --> 00:40:24,000
You stay at home.

518
00:40:26,010 --> 00:40:26,810
See you later.

519
00:40:36,560 --> 00:40:38,290
I still have to drive in the end.

520
00:40:38,890 --> 00:40:39,900
Why?

521
00:40:40,860 --> 00:40:41,960
I want to rest.

522
00:40:44,160 --> 00:40:45,900
This is too unfair to me.

523
00:40:46,320 --> 00:40:48,980
Just drive when it's your turn.

524
00:40:51,400 --> 00:40:52,430
Bro.

525
00:40:53,200 --> 00:40:54,730
I think your brother's mode

526
00:40:55,100 --> 00:40:57,200
is scarier than when he's scolding someone,

527
00:40:57,200 --> 00:40:59,060
fiercer than a dog being trained.

528
00:40:59,590 --> 00:41:01,430
He probably misses his wife.

529
00:41:02,330 --> 00:41:03,660
Why are you acting cool?

530
00:41:04,000 --> 00:41:05,730
I should have brought Phatsa.

531
00:41:06,330 --> 00:41:07,130
I can hear you.

532
00:41:07,960 --> 00:41:09,460
I'm not wrong.

533
00:41:09,950 --> 00:41:11,280
You're quite stubborn.

534
00:41:14,460 --> 00:41:15,320
By the way, bro.

535
00:41:17,300 --> 00:41:18,860
I want to ask you something.

536
00:41:19,900 --> 00:41:21,660
When I was caught back then,

537
00:41:22,600 --> 00:41:24,400
why did you believe it wasn't me?

538
00:41:25,960 --> 00:41:27,690
Because you said it wasn't you.

539
00:41:29,460 --> 00:41:30,560
Right, Nakhin?

540
00:41:32,560 --> 00:41:33,960
Your eyes already told us

541
00:41:34,530 --> 00:41:35,860
that you weren't lying.

542
00:41:36,730 --> 00:41:37,990
And most importantly,

543
00:41:38,760 --> 00:41:40,260
you are also our brother.

544
00:41:44,350 --> 00:41:45,490
I...

545
00:41:47,860 --> 00:41:49,730
I can be your brother, right?

546
00:41:50,930 --> 00:41:52,130
Of course, silly boy.

547
00:41:52,260 --> 00:41:54,660
You are also a member of the Devathitirat family.

548
00:41:54,660 --> 00:41:55,990
No matter what happens,

549
00:41:57,330 --> 00:41:58,600
you are our brother.

550
00:42:04,000 --> 00:42:08,200
You know, Dad used to tell me

551
00:42:09,130 --> 00:42:11,770
that I actually have two older brothers

552
00:42:11,790 --> 00:42:14,650
who are both powerful True Alphas and very awesome.

553
00:42:15,000 --> 00:42:18,540
One day, Dad told me

554
00:42:18,560 --> 00:42:20,930
he would bring me to live with you guys,

555
00:42:24,130 --> 00:42:26,300
to manage the family business together

556
00:42:26,300 --> 00:42:28,230
and protect this family together.

557
00:42:29,260 --> 00:42:31,790
I've always been looking forward to that day.

558
00:42:32,500 --> 00:42:34,530
If I weren't driving right now,

559
00:42:36,100 --> 00:42:38,160
I would have jumped up and hugged you.

560
00:42:43,860 --> 00:42:45,390
I'll tell you one more time.

561
00:42:47,160 --> 00:42:48,760
You are our younger brother.

562
00:42:50,300 --> 00:42:51,630
No matter what happens,

563
00:42:53,600 --> 00:42:55,260
we will always be on your side.

564
00:42:58,460 --> 00:43:01,960
That's a 'love you' without the word 'love'.

565
00:43:17,760 --> 00:43:19,000
Who called, bro?

566
00:43:21,400 --> 00:43:22,200
My wife.

567
00:43:24,260 --> 00:43:25,460
I wondered who it was.

568
00:43:28,560 --> 00:43:29,200
What's wrong?

569
00:43:29,200 --> 00:43:30,680
I'm sorry, Ms. Amintra.

570
00:43:30,710 --> 00:43:31,570
The thing is,

571
00:43:31,590 --> 00:43:33,110
the owner of that land is not available right now

572
00:43:33,110 --> 00:43:34,330
to let us go in and see the land.

573
00:43:34,330 --> 00:43:35,240
What?

574
00:43:36,110 --> 00:43:39,390
The owner informed me suddenly. I just found out too.

575
00:43:50,730 --> 00:43:54,460
Do you know how long it took me to get here?

576
00:43:54,480 --> 00:43:57,740
Or has the owner secretly sold the land to someone else?

577
00:43:58,010 --> 00:43:59,270
No, absolutely not.

578
00:43:59,300 --> 00:44:00,880
I can guarantee that there is currently no

579
00:44:00,880 --> 00:44:02,340
sales agreement reached.

580
00:44:04,060 --> 00:44:05,600
Then what exactly is going on?

581
00:44:05,600 --> 00:44:06,750
But there is another piece of land nearby.

582
00:44:06,750 --> 00:44:08,430
The location is better and more beautiful,

583
00:44:08,430 --> 00:44:11,290
and the owner is willing to let us go see it right now.

584
00:44:11,320 --> 00:44:13,510
Alright, since we're already here,

585
00:44:15,160 --> 00:44:17,820
send me the location. I'll head over right away.

586
00:44:17,930 --> 00:44:19,110
Okay, Ms. Amintra.

587
00:44:19,130 --> 00:44:20,730
I'll send it to you right now.

588
00:44:23,910 --> 00:44:28,360
Get some rest and remember to eat on time.

589
00:44:28,390 --> 00:44:32,110
As long as Phatsa is good, I will be good too.

590
00:44:35,360 --> 00:44:37,180
If you have time,

591
00:44:37,200 --> 00:44:40,100
take out that land information and have a look.

592
00:44:41,500 --> 00:44:45,180
I want us to focus on the purple and green areas,

593
00:44:45,200 --> 00:44:48,930
in case clients want to build industrial plants here in the future.

594
00:44:49,520 --> 00:44:52,010
Naphitch, where is the information?

595
00:44:55,360 --> 00:44:58,200
Wait, I think I forgot to bring it.

596
00:44:58,220 --> 00:45:01,020
I must have been in too much of a hurry just now, bro.

597
00:45:01,740 --> 00:45:03,680
But don't worry.

598
00:45:03,710 --> 00:45:07,040
I'll call the bodyguards at home to bring it over right away.

599
00:45:07,960 --> 00:45:10,960
But we don't have a single bodyguard at home right now.

600
00:45:12,060 --> 00:45:15,260
Then I'll drive over and deliver the information myself.

601
00:45:16,730 --> 00:45:26,010
Okay, I'll send you the location. Drive safely.

602
00:45:26,450 --> 00:45:27,250
Okay.

603
00:45:31,600 --> 00:45:33,080
Using work as an excuse,

604
00:45:33,500 --> 00:45:35,300
so there's no need to call again.

605
00:45:38,400 --> 00:45:39,730
What do we do next?

606
00:45:46,910 --> 00:45:48,110
What's wrong, honey?

607
00:45:48,380 --> 00:45:50,070
The original owner isn't selling anymore.

608
00:45:50,070 --> 00:45:54,040
What's going on? We've already driven out here.

609
00:45:54,060 --> 00:45:55,680
Probably out of their mind.

610
00:45:56,560 --> 00:45:57,630
But whatever.

611
00:45:57,650 --> 00:46:01,660
My agent said there's a new piece of land for sale.

612
00:46:01,840 --> 00:46:03,480
Why would you tell such important news

613
00:46:03,480 --> 00:46:05,010
to a competitor like me?

614
00:46:05,030 --> 00:46:06,740
Even if we are friends,

615
00:46:07,000 --> 00:46:09,250
competing with someone weaker than yourself

616
00:46:09,250 --> 00:46:10,570
is no fun.

617
00:46:10,590 --> 00:46:13,700
I prefer fair and evenly matched competition.

618
00:46:15,360 --> 00:46:18,420
I'll have Kingyok send you the location of the new land.

619
00:46:18,470 --> 00:46:19,270
Thanks.

620
00:46:20,390 --> 00:46:22,190
See you on the battlefield then.

621
00:46:27,370 --> 00:46:29,110
You didn't have to tell him.

622
00:46:30,660 --> 00:46:31,820
If you win against someone who from the very beginning

623
00:46:31,820 --> 00:46:33,010
doesn't even know the rules of the game,

624
00:46:33,010 --> 00:46:34,740
